Rpd8 out N016 {runit + (npd>=8 ? 0 : 1e9)}
Spd8 N016 vn pd 0 SWP
Sclk out N017 clk 0 SWP
Rclk N017 vn {rclamp}
Cgate out vn 350p
* +5 V DRIVE RAIL
* GATE NODE  -  this is what the driver charges
* OFF RAIL  -  0 V or -2 V
* INSIDE THE SEGMENTED GATE DRIVER  -  contents of models/segdrv.lib
* EIGHT PULL-UP SLICES  -  each 8 ohm, slice i on when npu >= i.  How hard the device is switched ON.
* EIGHT PULL-DOWN SLICES  -  each 8 ohm, slice i on when npd >= i.  How hard it is switched OFF.
* MILLER CLAMP  -  0.5 ohm
* the GaN gate
.model SWP SW(Ron=0.01 Roff=1e9 Vt=0.5 Vh=0.05)
.param npu=8 npd=8 runit=8 rclamp=0.5
.param VDRV=5 VNEG=0
Vvp vp 0 DC {VDRV}
Vvn vn 0 DC {VNEG}
Vpu pu 0 PULSE(0 1 0 1n 1n 200n 500n)
Vpd pd 0 PULSE(1 0 0 1n 1n 200n 500n)
Vclk clk 0 DC 0
.tran 0.1n 1u
.meas TRAN vgate_high MAX V(out)
* npu and npd are the slice counts the FPGA sets. Press Run to see the gate charge.
.backanno
.end
